course: dictionary
lesson: 12527
title: Despatch: sending something on its way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Despatch can be a verb or a noun. To despatch something means to send it off, especially a parcel, letter or message. A despatch is the sending itself, or an official report. Despatch is the British spelling of dispatch, so you may see both.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The shop will despatch your parcel tomorrow.» The shop is not keeping the parcel. It is sending it to you. The clue is parcel, something that travels. Ask yourself: what is being sent, and where is it going?
explain: Despatch can also mean to send a person to do a job, as in «The captain despatched a messenger with the news.» With despatch means quickly, as in «She answered the letter with despatch.» Use the words around it to choose the right meaning.
fact: Despatch means to send something off, especially a parcel, letter or message.
fact: A despatch is the sending itself, or an official report or message.
fact: «Your order has been despatched» is a message you may get from an online shop.
fact: «Mentioned in despatches» means a person was praised in an official report, often after a war.
fact: Despatch and dispatch mean the same thing; despatch is the British spelling.
exercise: «The shop will despatch your parcel tomorrow.» What does despatch mean here? | To keep it safe in the shop | To wrap it in paper | To open it carefully | *To send it off
exercise: «She answered the letter with despatch.» What does with despatch mean? | *Quickly | Without any words | Very slowly and carefully | Angrily
exercise: «The soldier was mentioned in despatches for his brave work.» What is a despatch in this sentence? | A small bird that sings at dawn | *An official report or message | A long walk through the hills | A kind of wooden box
test: «Mum asked me to despatch the letters before lunch.» What does despatch mean here? | To hide them in a drawer | *To send them off | To tear them up | To read them aloud
test: Which spelling is the British spelling of dispatch? | Dispatcher | *Despatch | Dispach | Dispatched and dispatching
exam: A despatch rider rides a motorbike to carry what? | Football boots | *Messages and letters | Sleeping bags | A cake to a party
